The course landing page shows a launch countdown and a "Related courses" panel:

function CourseLanding({ course }: { course: Course }) {
  const secondsLeft = useCountdown(course.publishedAt); // state, updated every second
  return (
    <>
      <LaunchBanner secondsLeft={secondsLeft} />
      <RelatedCourses query={{ category: course.category, exclude: course.id }} />
    </>
  );
}

function RelatedCourses({ query }: { query: RelatedQuery }) {
  const [related, setRelated] = useState<Course[]>([]);
  useEffect(() => {
    fetchRelated(query).then(setRelated);
  }, [query]);
  return <CourseRow courses={related} />;
}

Statement: "While the countdown runs, RelatedCourses sends a new GET /courses/related request about once per second, even though course never changes."

The course progress header:

function ProgressHeader({ lessons }: { lessons: LessonProgress[] }) {
  const [done, setDone] = useState(0);
  useEffect(() => {
    setDone(lessons.filter((l) => l.completed).length);
  }, [lessons]);
  return <h2>{done} / {lessons.length} lessons</h2>;
}

React DevTools Profiler, after a learner completes a lesson ("Record why each component rendered" enabled):

Commit 1  ProgressHeader  Why did this render? Props changed: (lessons)
Commit 2  ProgressHeader  Why did this render? Hook 1 changed

Statement: "Replacing the state and the effect with const done = lessons.filter((l) => l.completed).length; removes the second commit and still shows the correct count."

